(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-agent/src/core.asl#" :text "ASLF stage 1: the pure core of scripts/agentLoop/loop.py on the R1 host, byte for byte (gate tests/acceptance/r1AgentLoop/coreParityTest.sh): asnUnescape, parseForms (_parse_asn_forms), stripForms (_strip_top_level_forms), parseKv, parseReply, isProseWrapped, checkOwns, evidenceKey, mergeSpans, spanSeen, recordRead and renderSeen (the (:seen ...) coverage memory), renderWindow (the context window: each turn's forms nested raw, older turns append-only between compactions, the newest apart, and the ids of the turns it shows whole, which a repeated step may point at) and renderTranscript (a first message's window); and the reply shape of AGL13: nearestOp (alias or bounded edit distance), terminalForms, dataFindings (a scout reply of data forms as findings), uniqueSteps (a repeated step runs once); gateVerdict (rule gates: a gate run judged by its last (:gate ... :asserts n :failed m) line); noteStep (the session note: its text, the cap check and the (:note ...) slot). Strings are bytes on this host; every scan is byte-wise, which equals Python's character scan because every delimiter is ASCII and UTF-8 continuation bytes never are; lengths and cuts in renderWindow and ? in globs count code points. Known divergence: Python's Unicode \\s and \\w are ASCII here (whitespace is space and \\t..\\r; any byte from 0x80 counts as a word byte), and root paths are taken as absolute.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-agent/src/core.asl#firstOf" :text "the caller checked the bound; none traps")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-agent/src/core.asl#isProseWrapped" :text "more than 40 prose words")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-agent/src/core.asl#residueWordCount" :text "PROSE-THRESHOLD: words left outside the final top-level forms, no 40-word floor")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-agent/src/core.asl#hasFormResidue" :text "PROSE-THRESHOLD: true when forms parse but residueWordCount is still nonzero")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-agent/src/core.asl#joinForms" :text "PROSE-THRESHOLD: the text rebuilt from only its parsed top-level forms, residue dropped")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-agent/src/core.asl#checkOwns" :text "a path outside root is never owned")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-agent/src/core.asl#cutTurn" :text "old turns cut to 300 chars")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-agent/src/core.asl#renderWindow" :text "older turns stay append-only while they fit")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-agent/src/core.asl#runReadOnly" :text "a read-only command is an observation turn")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-agent/src/core.asl#harnessPath" :text "the loop state is not the task")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-agent/src/core.asl#hiddenPath" :text "an eval answer key is not the task")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-agent/src/core.asl#runOutward" :text "push, publish, request bodies, outside moves need confirmation")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-agent/src/coreCli.asl#" :text "asl-host run asl/packages/asl-agent/src/coreCli.asl CORPUS: reads netstring cases (<len>:<bytes>; kind, field count, fields) and prints one line per case, <index> <kind> <result>, in the serialisation of tests/acceptance/r1AgentLoop/coreParity.py. scripts/agentLoop/loop.py sends its batches here on /dev/stdin (ASLF stage 2); the kinds window, strip, kv, key, seen, spanSeen, reads, steps, dataFindings, nearest, terminal, gate, note, outward, changePlan, repair and the LP2 claims kinds and LP3 retry/advisor kinds (extractClaims receiptBacks isBacked isProseClaimBacked turnBringsEvidence forgetCutEvidence isTurnObservation unwrapReadTxns mergeFindings wrongCitationNote hasNegatorNear extractProseStrings collectProseStrings batchingRates costForm escalationNear reinforceWhyFor nowForm noWriteNudge gateNow buildRetryBrief advisorSkip parseAdvice parseSpecVerdict digestLine evidenceDigest advisorGateOutput advisorOpLine advisorSummary) and the LP4 gate kinds (gateVerdicts vacuousOutsideOwns isSwallowedExceptLine isPassLine isSingleLineSwallow findSwallowedInAdded scanSwallowed placeholderHit missingGatePaths missingGateFiles gateRunScripts gatePartitionFiles gateVacuousMessage gateRevertVerdict) and LP3b loop kinds (sessionHeader endStatus finalGatesGreen preserveFiles handBackRestore loopBoundary) serve it")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-agent/src/coreCli.asl#gateFromFields" :text "a gate is 6 flat fields: cmd exit(-1=none) timeout(0/1) seconds(-1=none) stdout stderr")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-agent/src/coreCli.asl#receiptFromFields" :text "a receipt is 15 flat fields: id op kind cmd stdout file path symbol query topic url exit(-1=none) status error content")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-agent/src/coreCli.asl#kvIntFromFields" :text "a \"kv int\" pair is 2 flat fields: key count")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-agent/src/coreCli.asl#parseGateRuns" :text "---- claims.asl wire adapters: flat count-prefixed encodings, consumed left to right ----")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-agent/src/coreCli.asl#parseOneKeyFields" :text "a key is a count-prefixed list of (tag \"i\"|\"s\", value) pairs, matching c/evidenceKey's (List KvVal)")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-agent/src/diff.asl#" :text "Pure ASL unified diff and similarity ratio replacing Python difflib in agentLoop: unifiedDiff byte-identical to difflib.unified_diff, ratio equal to SequenceMatcher(None, a, b).ratio() with matching autojunk semantics above 200 elements and longest-matching-block recursion under 200 elements.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-agent/src/diff.asl#Sm" :text "O(1) arrays; the prelude Map is a list")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-agent/src/diff.asl#makeSm" :text "difflib b2j with autojunk, as CSR over line ids")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-agent/src/exec.asl#" :text "Leon's op dispatch and receipt text, ported from scripts/agentLoop/loop.py (parity: asl/packages/asl-agent/tests/execParityTest.asl against asl/packages/asl-agent/tests/genExecFixture.py): execOp! (execute_op: intent, the effects registry, gate, run as a declared gate, hidden and harness paths, run read hints, run, delete, manage, note, the write and edit prechecks, txn, flush after persisted writes, git ops, done, tree with harness entries hidden, the asl ops, evidence, findings, escalate, raw and recorded), execGateOp!, intentReceipt, execNoteOp, hideHarnessEntries, hiddenTouched, harnessTouched and opWords; formatOpReceipt, formatGateRun, gateTail and gateOutcome (format_op_receipt and its gate helpers); opShapes (_OP_SHAPES), acceptedOpsForMode (get_accepted_ops_for_mode), terminalForms and undeclaredAnswer; collectProseStrings (_collect_prose_strings). The sub-executors are the ported modules: aslOps (asl ops over an injected run), txn, gitOps (git ops and gate runs), runOps (run, delete, manage over the Procs table this module threads). A receipt is the ordered field list of the Python dict (Receipt of Val). Globals the Python read (_receipt_id, _snapshot_before_write, the _WRITTEN journal, _READ_CAP, _RUN_TIMEOUT, _RUN_DEADLINE, _SESSION_ENV, ASL_EVAL_HIDDEN_VARS and the hidden variables' values) are ExecEnv fields and hook functions. Known divergences: an int :argv or :cmd is taken as its digits where the Python raised TypeError; a receipt missing a field format_op_receipt indexes (lines, totalChars, cmd) formats that field as None where the Python raised KeyError; a note answer the core could not produce is a rejected ERR_CORE_HOST_MALFORMED receipt where the Python raised; regex \\s and \\w are ASCII (any byte from 0x80 is a word byte), as in the core.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-agent/src/exec.asl#rawRequiredBytes" :text "loop.py RAW_REQUIRED_BYTES")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-agent/src/exec.asl#noteMaxChars" :text "loop.py NOTE_MAX_CHARS, about 600 to 800 tokens")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-agent/src/exec.asl#recSet" :text "dict assignment: an existing key keeps its place")
