(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-agent/src/gitOps.asl#" :text "Leon's git ops, gate IO and gate preflight ported from scripts/agentLoop/loop.py (_run_bounded, _is_path_in_repo, _line_arg, git_slice, _git_next_form, _exec_git_op, run_gates, gate_preflight, format_gate_preflight, _changed_owned_files; parity fixture tests/parity/agentLoop/genGitOpsFixture.py). git and sh run through procSpawnv argv lists in their own process group; a timeout kills the group. Child output is read as bytes and newline-translated like Python text mode (\\r\\n and \\r become \\n). A receipt is an ordered field list in the key order of the Python dict. Known divergences: invalid UTF-8 stays as bytes (Python writes U+FFFD); strip and splitlines treat only ASCII whitespace and the ASCII, U+0085, U+2028 and U+2029 separators; realpath does not follow a dangling symlink; OSError text is rebuilt from the errno kind.")
