(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-agent/src/retry.asl#" :text "Leon's retry brief, escalation, cost and advisor text builders ported from scripts/agentLoop/loop.py (unit LP3). Ported: buildRetryBrief, costForm, batchingRates, reinforceWhyFor, escalationNear, nowForm, noWriteNudge, gateNow, advisorSummary, advisorSkip, parseAdvice, parseSpecVerdict, digestLine, evidenceDigest, advisorGateOutput, advisorOpLine. Skipped: _vendor_bounds and _fit_vendor_call stay Python; both read and write a live provider object's timeout/queue_timeout attributes (getattr/setattr on an opaque host object), which is a side effect on external mutable state, not a pure computation, so they have no ASL form here. buildRetryBrief takes pre-rendered text for the pieces that need root_dir file reads or the giant format_op_receipt/evidence_form serialisers (describe_parse_failure, undeclared_answer, get_accepted_ops_for_mode, format_op_receipt, evidence_form): loop.py still computes those and passes the resulting strings in, the same way it already passes serialised plan state to plan.asl. Rounding: batchingRates and costForm's opsPerTurn/singleOpShare are ratios of small non-negative counts, rounded to 2 decimals by exact integer round-half-to-even (numerator*100 divided by denominator), which matches Python's round(ops/turns,2) for every count pair since both sides start from the same IEEE754 division of small integers; secPerTurn rounds a genuine elapsed-seconds float to 1 decimal by scaling in Float64 and rounding half to even, which can diverge from Python's round() only at the rare double-precision boundary Python's own docs call out (e.g. round(2.675,2)); stringFromFloat64 itself already renders the shortest round-trip decimal, matching Python repr. Strings are scanned byte-wise except where Python len()/slicing is character-based (target and text-field truncation), where stringChars is used instead. Since F1 (rebased onto main 63ad6546): digestLine appends a whitespace-collapsed, 100-char :excerpt from a read's content or a run's stdout, so ReceiptRec carries a 15th field, content.")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-agent/src/retry.asl#retryTurn!" :text "number of completed retries; delay values and budgetLeft are seconds.\nRetry provider failures only for the vendor transient classes. retryCount is the")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-agent/src/retry.asl#hintedPause" :text "the pause for a server Retry-After hint in seconds, shared by retryTurn! and the pool: none when the raw hint reaches the wall budget left (no retry), else the hint clipped to retryAfterCapSec (300)")
(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-agent/src/retry.asl#slice":text "-- small string/char primitives, self-contained (byte-wise unless noted) --")
