(:doc :symbol "asl/packages/asl-agent/src/runOps.asl#" :text "Leon's run, manage and delete ops and the run git guard, ported from scripts/agentLoop/loop.py (_check_run_git_guard, _exec_run_op, _exec_manage_op, _exec_delete_op, _run_outward, run_read_only, hidden_vars, _spawn, _kill_spawned, _settle, _tree_snapshot, _worktree_files, _pre_bytes, rebase_written, inside_root; parity fixture tests/parity/agentLoop/genRunOpsFixture.py). The asl-engine process table behind (:manage ...) becomes the Procs value this module threads: a command runs as /bin/sh -c CMD through procSpawnv in its own process group, only the user's command string goes to sh -c, stdout and stderr are read into one log, and a kill (and a run timeout) sends SIGTERM to the group, waits up to 100 ms and sends SIGKILL to the group. Tail lines pass the wire relativization of scripts/aslForms.py (the root, its real path and the tool root become relative) as the transport did; an engine refusal keeps the text the loop saw (the last 300 characters of the wire line). git listings go through gitOps runBounded; blob bytes and the process table read pipes raw. Receipt ids, the session name, the step timeout, the hidden variable names, the tool root and the journal (onKeep, snap) are parameters owned by other units. Known divergences: a process table lives for one Leon run, not across engine restarts; stdout and stderr chunks that arrive in the same poll window are ordered stdout first; invalid UTF-8 stays as bytes (Python reads U+FFFD); a background child of a finished command is not signalled and its pipes are drained only when an op or drainProcs runs; the log keeps its last 1 MiB; a kill always ends with SIGKILL to the group, where the engine sent it only while the leader lived; strip, split and the regex \\s and \\w treat ASCII (and 0x1c-0x1f for whitespace) only; file change detection uses size, whole-second mtime and bytes (a file modified in the snapshot's second is compared by bytes); a failure the original raised as an exception (settle IO, journal refusal, remove) is a rejected receipt.")
